Atelier is an independent Anki desktop add-on by Daedalus Works.
Root Atelier code uses its supplied MIT license. This combined distribution retains
Exam Sprout 0.10.1 under sprout/LICENSE and embedded Card Studio / Workshop under
workshop/LICENSE, with integration changes described by the current source kit.
The bundled PDF text parser retains its license at workshop/vendor/pypdf/LICENSE.
This release uses pypdf 6.21.1, with package imports adjusted only for namespace
isolation. Adobe Core 14 metric-data permission is retained in the parser's
_codecs/core_font_metrics.py notice; no font binaries are distributed.

Anki, Qt, Chromium, Onigiri, IO Enhanced, HyperTTS, Contanki and shared-deck services
remain separate software. Their binaries, fonts, configuration and user data are not
bundled. No official endorsement or universal compatibility is claimed.

Pip artwork/model/animation assets and the card-builder book artwork remain from the
supplied packages. World scenery comes from the accepted cumulative Atelier build.
No font files, runtime CDN or automatic tracking are included. Optional provider
assistance requires explicit configuration and consent; see PRIVACY.md.

Embedded upstream README/verification documents are preserved as provenance, not
current installation instructions or fresh verification. Follow the top-level
RELEASE-NOTES.md and the version-matched verification report for this combined build.
